# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; never commit a resolved value.
# fiddle.toml references only the NAME of this variable, never its value.
LITELLM_API_KEY=

# M2's GitHub effects. A fine-grained token whose repository selection is
# peel/fiddle-effects-acceptance and nothing else. Deliberately not a classic
# `repo` token: this one is structurally incapable of touching peel/fiddle or
# peel/fiddle-acceptance, and a ref-create against either answers
# `403 Resource not accessible by personal access token`.
#
# That selection is a measured fact rather than an intention. The probe table in
# docs/technical/effects-repository.md records 200 on this repository's
# /collaborators and 403 on both others — and the selection was two repositories
# wide until 2026-08-10, when it was narrowed. scripts/live-github.sh re-reads
# that 200 on every run and refuses a target the selection does not include.
#
# The permissions, and what each one is for:
#
#   Contents        read and write — push the branch
#   Pull requests   read and write — open the pull request
#   Actions         read and write — POST .../dispatches, i.e. THE DISPATCH.
#                                    A dispatch 403 is this permission missing.
#                                    It is not `Workflows`; see below.
#   Metadata        read only      — mandatory on every fine-grained token, and
#                                    what answers the /collaborators probe
#   Secrets         none           — asserted on every run: if the credential can
#                                    enumerate the target's secrets the lane
#                                    fails and says it is scoped too broadly
#
# `Workflows` read and write is a different permission with a different job: it
# is what a push touching `.github/workflows/**` requires. That is how the
# target's own fiddle-check.yml was installed, and it is not something this lane
# ever does — the only file it pushes is a one-line probe at the repository root.
# So grant `Workflows` to a credential that maintains that workflow file, and not
# to this one: a lane credential able to rewrite the target's CI holds authority
# nothing here uses.
#
# This covers the local lane only. The dispatch-only Actions lane reads the same
# value from the FIDDLE_EFFECTS_TOKEN repository secret, because a local file
# never reaches a runner; that secret needs exactly this list.
FIDDLE_GITHUB_TOKEN=
